country music's biggest stars returned  to las vegas last night for the 57th  annual academy of country music awards  and let me just say it didn't disappoint  from the fashion to the performances and  history-making wins we need to break it  all down  yes so for the first time ever the show  was held at allegiant stadium hosted by  the one and only dolly parton along with  rising stars gabby barrett and jimmy  allen among some of the notable winners  old dominion took home group of the year  for the fifth year in a row  carly pierce earned female artist of the  year and miranda lambert won the biggest  honor of the night entertainer of the  year for the first time that's right it  was definitely a really great night for  the ladies but morgan wallen  who sparked debate after winning album  of the year for dangerous the double  album one year after his major  controversy morgan was banned from the  acms in 2021 after he was caught on  camera in a leaked video using a racial  racial slur  yeah so morgan was also pulled from  several radio stations and suspended  from his record label in addition he was  deemed ineligible at the 2021 cmt awards  banned from the 2021 billboard music  awards and banned from any  non-collaborative categories at the cma  awards morgan has since apologized on  several occasions and appeared on good  morning america back in the summer where  he revealed he checked into a rehab  center after the incident now morgan  released the album in january of 2021  just weeks before all the controversy  the album has gone on to make history  spending more weeks in the top 10 of the  billboard 200 chart than any other  country album ever a record previously  held by taylor swift  yeah while morgan received loud cheers  inside the stadium not everyone was in  support of the win with maren morris  reportedly refusing to applaud or stand  up for the singer mind you i saw the  clip and she did see here's the clip  right here so she could see she's in a  conversation and then very faint in the  back you see her clapping so i don't  know  where all the rumors are coming from but  many disappointed twitter users claim  the win suggests that racism is  celebrated in country music while others  pointed out that morgan apologized and  shouldn't have to sacrifice his career  here's what morgan had to say during his  acceptance speech  when i started this album  i was a kid  by the time i put it out i was a father  and that's become more important to me  than anything else  to my son this album and this award will  signify that his daddy was a fighter and  then he chased his dreams and worked  hard to make them a reality i'd also  like to thank my good lord and savior  jesus christ my family  my close friends  my band  my team in nashville country radio and  everyone who has shown me grace along  the way  now fellow country singer hardy spoke  with entertainment tonight shortly after  the win admitting he cried when he heard  morgan's name he explained  it means a lot for him he works very  hard he deserves that award for those  who don't know your peers or  co-workers vote for who should win this  award hardy added that everybody  deserves a second chance deserves a  chance to fight for themselves and  that's exactly what's happened so this  was bigger than that award for him it  meant a lot and i'm very proud of him  yeah um i mean listen first of all award  shows in general are a lot of politics  you know payola friends of friends this  person you know awards don't really it  just seems like the country music world  has forgiven morgan wallin oh at least  these awards have forgiven morgan wall  and i'd be interested to see what other  award shows are gonna do like the  billboards the grammys things like that  um  i just  racism has always been a thing in  country music unfortunately and so has  sexism like you see a lot of women  country singers um they don't get the  same amount of play on radio stations  they don't get this the same amount of  love as their male counterparts so  there's a lot of like issues in country  music i mean i'm sure a lot of genres  have issues but  at this point i'll be honest with you i  was actually surprised morgan got  cancelled  to begin with because country music  yeah because i'm like  i didn't think country music uh as a  whole really cared too much about  something like this to be quite honest  with you i was shocked that they took a  stance i mean it only lasted 10 months  um but you know it's it's tough i feel  like  i believe in country i believe in cancel  culture when there's racism when there's  sexism when there's just you know  discrimination when there's violence  when there's things like that i feel  like people need to be checked and need  to be humbled and be held accountable  but i also believe in the power of  forgiveness and things being a teachable  moment i don't know if morgan  has learned anything i don't know i  don't know him personally i just know  that he has apologized i found the  apologies to be insincere um but i don't  know it's one of those things like i'm  not god i can't judge him i i don't know  what he's learned i  yeah the whole situation is just  wild but i get why people are mad and i  get why people are supporting him so i  don't know what are you thinking  you're like i can see this and i can see  listen what i would have liked  i like that he went away to rehab and he  took a beat to learn and to hopefully  grow listen what what i really wanted to  see when he was up there in that speech  is to talk a little bit about what  you've learned and how you've grown  because that was a really great  opportunity to speak out and to speak up  and to be humble and to talk about where  you've changed and i wanted i wanted to  see that so but again time will tell  right you talk about giving people the  room to grow and be better i want i want  people in this world advocating for  everyone and to grow if we push them  under a rock and they get you know i  don't want i want more people  spreading love and doing good things and  if he's willing to do that and be out in  the world and be a part of that that's  what i want to see  but he should have done that when he  gave a  speech you know  yeah i do agree i think it would have  been nice for him i mean he didn't have  to make the whole speech about that  moment but it would have been nice if he  said you know you know this is a  celebration for all my fans and and how  far i've come or something on those  lines where you're like ah you know  where you kind of want to root for him  yes but it's just one of those things  like i understand cancel culture but at  the same time i'm like how long do we  cancel a person and and who judges  if they've learned or not if they've if  they if they're remorseful like how do  we even merit that so the whole thing is  just insane but at the end of the day  it's an award show it's politics i mean  i don't know if i care about awards as  much as anything you know  um fair enough yeah that's my thought
 

